                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Manufacturing Automation" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Manufacturing Automation" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Manufacturing Automation Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>Manufacturers may face repetitive manual work, process delays, data-entry errors, disconnected applications, and limited visibility into workflow status.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Repetitive Manual Tasks: Identify high-volume repetitive activities and automate them using structured workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Process Delays: Automate approvals, notifications, reminders, and escalations.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Data Entry Errors: Use integrated workflows and validation to reduce repetitive manual data entry.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Disconnected Applications: Connect systems so information can move automatically between business processes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Limited Workflow Visibility: Use dashboards, logs, and alerts to monitor automated process performance.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Manufacturing Automation</b></h3>
                <p>Each manufacturer has different business rules, processes, systems, approval structures, and operational requirements. Custom automation helps fit workflows to the organization.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Customize Automation Workflows: Build automation around the organization's actual manufacturing and business processes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Create Role-Based Workspaces: Give teams visibility into automated tasks, approvals, exceptions, and process status.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Automate Notifications: Configure alerts, reminders, approvals, and escalation workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Build Automation Dashboards: Provide insights into workflow volume, processing times, exceptions, and performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Gather User Feedback: Continuously refine automated processes based on user and business feedback.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

